cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "incline: Comprehensive Trend Estimation for Noisy Time Series"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-06"
url: "https://github.com/finite-sample/incline"
repository-code: "https://github.com/finite-sample/incline"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/incline/"
abstract: >-
  A Python package for estimating the trend at a point in a noisy time series, with
  calibrated uncertainty. Smooths the series and differentiates the smooth, and reports a
  standard error for every estimate: exact for linear smoothers, from the posterior for
  Gaussian processes and state-space models, and bootstrapped otherwise. Includes
  Savitzky-Golay filters, splines, LOESS, local polynomials, L1 trend filtering,
  multi-scale analysis (SiZer) and seasonal decomposition. Coverage is verified by
  Monte Carlo against known truth.
keywords:
  - time-series
  - derivative
  - slope
  - trend
  - savitzky-golay
  - spline
  - gaussian-process
  - kalman-filter
  - robust-statistics
  - multiscale-analysis
